    "body": "examples/musig.c is the only example that handles secret keys without\nrandomizing the context, which secp256k1.h highly recommends. Randomize\nit as schnorr.c does.\n\nschnorr.c erases the secret key buffer after use, but the keypair holds\na copy of the secret key and stayed on the stack. Erase it too.\n\n",
